# The multiplicity-sensitive ideal of a point of `Symⁿ C` (area SY, `divOf`)

## The defect of the naive characteristic-polynomial criterion

Let `V ⊆ C` be an affine open and `p` a point of `Symⁿ C` in the chart of `U = Vⁿ`, with
`φ : A = Γ(Cⁿ,Vⁿ)^{S_n} → F` the induced map, and let `x : Fin n → C(F')` be a lift of `p`
over a field extension `F'`.  The key lemma (`ChartPt.φ_eq_evalMap`) gives
`χ_b := φ (∏_m (T - b^(m))) = ∏_m (T - b(x_m)) ∈ F[T]` for `b ∈ Γ(C,V)`.

The condition `χ_b = T^n` is equivalent to `b(x_m) = 0` **for all `m`**, which is insensitive to
how often a point is repeated: for `C = ℙ¹`, `n = 2` and the diagonal lift `x_0 = x_1 = z` the
divisor of `p` is `2[z]` but `{b | χ_b = T²} = m_z` is the *reduced* divisor ideal, not
`m_z²`.  So `{b | χ_b = T^n}` is **not** the ideal of the divisor (see the note at the end of
`Submission/Work/SymQuot/NOTES.md`).

## The correct criterion

The order of vanishing of `b ∈ Γ(C,V)` at a point `z` of the support can still be read off from
`φ`:  for `b` ranging over `Γ(C,V)` and `χ_b ∈ F[T]` as above, the elements
`χ_b(b) := ∏_m (b - b(x_m)) ∈ Γ(C_F, W)` (the value of the polynomial `χ_b` at the section `b`,
which is `F`-rational and computable from `φ` alone) satisfy

* `ord_z (χ_b(b)) ≥ D(z)` for **every** `b`, because each factor `b - b(x_m)` with `x_m = z`
  lies in `m_z`; and
* `ord_z (χ_b(b)) = D(z)` for **some** `b`, namely one with `b - b(z) ∉ m_z²` (such a `b`
  exists because `m_z/m_z²` is generated by the images of the `b - b(z)`, by flatness of `F/K`
  and Nakayama).

Hence `D(z) = min_b ord_z (χ_b(b))`, i.e. the divisor of `p` is cut out by the ideal generated
by the values `χ_b(b)`:

* `sectionsAlgebraMap C W : F →+* Γ(C,W)` — the structure map making the sections of a curve
  over `F` an `F`-algebra;
* `charIdeal F d` — the ideal of `Γ(C_F, bcOpens F d.V)` generated by the `χ_b(b)`,
  `b ∈ Γ(C, d.V)`.

The divisor of `p` is `divisorOfIdeal (charIdeal F d)`.
-/
import Submission.Work.SymQuot.DivOf.IdealData

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

-- Lean v4.35.0-rc3 / Mathlib 5e0c4e5 made `isDefEq` respect transparency when unifying instances; with it,
-- `ZMod.instField` and `ZMod.commRing` (and `Neg (ZMod p)` via `SubtractionMonoid`) no longer unify, which
-- breaks `ring`/`rw`/module-instance search on `ZMod p`. Restore the v4.34 behaviour for this file.


set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry
open scoped Classical

universe u

namespace Work.SymQuot.DivOf

open Work.CurveBasics

variable {F : Type u} [Field F]

/-- **The structure map `F →+* Γ(C,W)`** making the sections of a curve `C` over `F` over an open
`W` an `F`-algebra: the pullback of the structure morphism `C ⟶ Spec F` followed by the
identification `Γ(Spec F) ≅ F`. -/
noncomputable def sectionsAlgebraMap (C : Curve F) (W : C.left.Opens) : F →+* Γ(C.left, W) :=
  (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of F)).inv ≫ C.hom.appTop ≫
    C.left.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)).op).hom)

variable {K : Type u} [Field K]

/-- **The multiplicity-sensitive ideal of a point of `Symⁿ C`**: the ideal of the affine ring
`Γ(C_F, bcOpens F V)` generated by the values `χ_b(b)` of the characteristic polynomials of the
sections `b ∈ Γ(C,V)` at `b` itself.  Its divisor (`divisorOfIdeal`) is the divisor of the
point. -/
noncomputable def charIdeal {C : Curve K} {n : ℕ} [NeZero n] [CurveAffineCover C]
    (F : Type u) [Field F] [Algebra K F] {p : Work.SpecLin.FPt (Sym C n) F}
    (d : ChartPt C n p) : Ideal Γ((C.baseChange F).left, C.bcOpens F d.V) :=
  Ideal.span (Set.range fun b : Γ(C.left, d.V) =>
    Polynomial.eval₂ (sectionsAlgebraMap (C.baseChange F) (C.bcOpens F d.V))
      (((Curve.baseChangeFst C F).app d.V).hom b) (d.charpolyValue b))

end Work.SymQuot.DivOf
